From 49414def85a91a7e780af58d43af7e5a6bc6c8a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:14:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Examples: behaviour libraries for the CPU and the GPU, placed
 by --execution

All the examples (and the Robin test of ex8, which now declares the
options of mfem-mgis) build their behaviour libraries with the CMake
function mfem_mgis_add_behaviours_library of mfem-mgis: for the CPU
(generic interface) and, if MFEM uses a GPU, for the GPU (generic-parallel
interface). Their option -l (-lU and -lA for ex8) gives a library; by
default, the library placed by the option --execution of mfem-mgis is used
(mfem_mgis::getBehavioursLibrary). The variants MUMPS and PETSc of ex4 get
the option -l.

Tests on a GPU (option MFEM_MGIS_EXAMPLES_GPU_TESTS, for MFEM compiled with
CUDA or HIP): --execution gpu for the examples using the solvers of hypre or
of MFEM, --execution mixed --linear-solver-device cpu for the ones using
MUMPS or UMFPack, and variants with the behaviours or the finite elements
on the CPU (14 tests). The GPU variants of ex8 replace the ones selecting
the device and the computations by kernels with environment variables. The
MTest file of ex8 and a profiling script load the new libraries.

READMEs: the option --execution, and the commands of ex7 and ex8 on a GPU.
Tests: 24/24 on the CPU, 14/14 on the GPU.
